cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these results or kernels, please cite this repository and the Selective Attention paper."
title: "Selective-Attention-Study: Selective Attention trained like Dilution-Attention at 16K context"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Royer-Research-Labs/Selective-Attention-Study"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  A companion study to Dilution-Attention. Selective Attention (Leviathan, Kalman and Matias, ICLR 2025) is
  trained with no position signal at 209M parameters and 16K context under the same recipe as the
  Dilution-Attention runs, with a fused Triton kernel for training and cached decoding. The repository holds the
  kernel, the training harness, run records, and evaluations of in-context loss, needle-in-a-haystack retrieval
  out to 128K, harder retrieval with natural filler and distractors, and long-document use of distant context.
keywords:
  - selective attention
  - attention
  - length extrapolation
  - long context
  - triton
  - transformer
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
